;;; Ein — bug repro
;;;
;;; `TypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'str' and 'int'`
;;; from `apriori.layer_1`, on a KB that is otherwise perfectly well-formed.
;;;
;;; The bug. `apriori.layer_1` opens the commitment search with
;;; `sorted(alive)`, where each element is a `FactId` — `(relation_name,
;;; args)`. Tuple comparison walks into `args`, so two candidates of the same
;;; relation whose slot *i* holds a `str` in one and an `int` in the other are
;;; incomparable and CPython raises. `canon.state_key` avoids exactly this with
;;; `key=repr`; `apriori` does not.
;;;
;;; Why it needs an hrule. Blind hypothesis generation cannot reach it:
;;; `hypgen._raw_candidates` builds candidates out of `kb.names`, and
;;; `store.rebuild_indexes` only enters an arg into that index
;;; `if isinstance(a, str)` — so every blind candidate is all-strings. An
;;; `hrule` has no such filter: its `:assert` args come from *bindings*, and a
;;; variable that matched an int arg carries the int through. Hence the shape
;;; below — one `hrule`, one variable, two facts that bind it to `1` and to
;;; `left`.
;;;
;;; Status: **not fixed, pinned.** This is M1a hazard H2
;;; (`plans/m1a_rust/design/02_determinism_and_order.md` §5) and open question
;;; Q-M1a.4. ein.rs's `Value` is totally ordered by construction and cannot
;;; raise, so on this input the two implementations must differ: one crashes,
;;; one answers. Fixing ein.py to sort by `repr` here would change the
;;; candidate order of every puzzle to buy nothing any real puzzle has asked
;;; for. So the crash is recorded rather than repaired, and the corpus carries
;;; it in the `crash-parity` group (Q-M1a.14).
;;;
;;; One more thing this fixture showed, which changed that group's comparison
;;; rule: the message itself is not stable. Which operand lands on the left of
;;; the failing `<` depends on the `frozenset` iteration order inside `sorted`,
;;; so across `PYTHONHASHSEED` values ein.py alternates between
;;; `'str' and 'int'` and `'int' and 'str'`. A crash is therefore compared by
;;; exit code and exception *class*, never by its message.
;;;
;;; Pinned by `corpus/corpus.toml` (the sweep runs it under every declared
;;; run, against a banked exit golden) and by `ein-infer/tests/interning.rs`,
;;; which uses it for a second thing: `Ann` is a name only the compiler ever
;;; sees. It was `ein.py/tests/inference/test_mixed_type_hypothesis.py` until
;;; M1a S1a.10.2.

(relation slotval T T)
(relation seat    T T)

;; The two bindings. `?v` matches the int 1 from one and the symbol `left`
;; from the other, and both reach `alive` as candidate `seat` facts.
(slotval x 1)
(slotval y left)

(hrule guess ()
  :match  (slotval ?k ?v)
  :assert (seat Ann ?v)
  :why    "guess that Ann sits at {?v}")

(query
  :goal   (seat Ann ?s)
  :hrules (guess)
)
